name,key,title,bio,keywords
Areeba Khalid,areeba,"BS, Mathematics & MS, Applied Mathematics/Data Science, Adelphi University","Areeba Khalid is the Director of Graduate Business Programs in the Robert B. Willumstad School of Business at Adelphi University, an adjunct professor, and a doctoral student in Learning Sciences. Her research interests include technology-supported learning, mathematical problem solving, and generative AI in higher education, with a focus on how learners use and evaluate AI as part of the learning process.","Mathematics Education, Problem Solving, Generative AI, Educational Technology, Learning Sciences"
Grace Qi Hu,grace,"MA Educational Technology, Adelphi University","Grace Hu is a doctoral student in Learning Sciences at Adelphi University. Her research focuses on teaching expertise in makerspaces. Her broader interests include instructional design, accessibility, and the thoughtful integration of generative AI in education.","Teaching Expertise, Makerspace, Instructional Design, Accessibility, Artificial Intelligence"
Jennifer Southard,jen,"MS English Education, Hofstra University; MA Educational Technology, Adelphi University","Jennifer Southard is the Assistant Director of the Faculty Center for Professional Excellence at Adelphi University, adjunct professor, and Adelphi University PhD candidate. Her research examines how writing is shifting from a static response to an immediate exigency into a distributed, sense-making process among human, technological, and environmental agent, redefining AI as a partner in co-composition to better prepare writers for increasingly complex, post-human communication milieus.","Instructional Design, Writing and Composition Studies, Artificial Intelligence, Digital Literacy, Learning Sciences"
Ryan Foley ,ryan,"BS in Marketing, Masters of Business Administration, Certificate in Human Resource Management , Adelphi University ",Ryan Foley is the Director of Undergraduate Programs in the Robert B Willumstad School of Business at Adelphi University and a doctoral student in Learning Sciences. His research includes the embodied experiences of learning as related to the arts and how these learning practices can applied to other domains. ,"Embodied Learning, The Arts, Arts Education, Business , Business Education, Aesthetics "
Salih Mansur,salih,"BA Electronic Design and Multimedia, City College of New York (CUNY); BA Forensic Psychology, John Jay; MA Communication Arts, NYIT; MS Instructional Technology & MS Artificial Intelligence Systems, Touro","Salih is a Communications Officer @ Design & Technology SIG (AERA). His interests lie at the intersection of artificial intelligence, educational technology, and the psychology of learning, with a focus on human-centered AI and digital literacy.","Artificial Intelligence, Learning Sciences, Digital Literacy, Educational Technology"
Sultana Yasmeen Jamal,sultana,"BBA Business Studies, American College of Dubai; MBA Human Resource Management, East Delta University","Sultana Yasmeen Jamal is a doctoral student in Learning Sciences at Adelphi University. She brings over a decade of experience in education and instructional leadership across Bangladesh and the United Arab Emirates, with a focus on early childhood and primary education. Her research interests include AI-supported instructional design for multilingual learners, inclusive education, and equity in educational technology.","Translanguaging, AI-Supported Educational Technology, Equity in Education, Curriculum Design"
Erin Puglisi,erin,"BS in Corporate Communications and Psychology Susquehanna University, MS Digital Marketing Sacred Heart University","Erin Puglisi is an adjunct professor of marketing at Sacred Heart University and a doctoral student in Learning Sciences at Adelphi University. Her research interests lie at the intersection of generative AI, neurodiversity, and teaching and learning in higher education, with a focus on how AI can support diverse learners and educators. Her broader interests include experiential and play-based learning, instructional design, and innovative approaches to teaching marketing.",
Jared Mroz,jared,"BA English, Literature and Rhetoric, Binghamton University 1998
MS Business Analytics, Adelphi University 2022
MBA Business Administration, Adelphi University 2026","Jared Mroz is an Executive Director at Morgan Stanley, an Adjunct Professor in the Wilumstad School of Business at Adelphi University, as well as an Adjunct Professor in the Business School at Molloy University. He is a doctoral student in Learning Sciences at Adelphi University with a research interest in the role of music in learning and cognition, artificial intelligence, as well as developing and suporting learning in a professional technology setting. ","Artificial Intelligence, AI, Machine Learning, Music, Professional Development, Learning Sciences"
Gabriella Deninno,gab,"BA in Mathematics, MSEd in Mathematics Education with STEM integration, Hofstra University",Gabriella Deninno is a computer science teacher at Mineola UFSD and a doctoral student in Learning Sciences. Her research interests include embodied learning as it relates to mental representation building in K-12 computer science and mathematics education. ,"Embodied Learning, Computer Science Education, Mathematics Education, Learning Sciences, Educational Technology, Curriculum Design"
